== SERIAL MARKERS EMITTED BY DRIVER ==

VIRTIO_GPU_PCI           — PCI device discovered (1af4:1050), IRQ assigned
VIRTIO_GPU_QUEUES        — controlq + cursorq configured
VIRTIO_GPU_DISPLAY_INFO  — GET_DISPLAY_INFO succeeded, scanout mode reported
VIRTIO_GPU_CREATE_2D     — RESOURCE_CREATE_2D succeeded
VIRTIO_GPU_ATTACH_BACKING — RESOURCE_ATTACH_BACKING succeeded
VIRTIO_GPU_SCANOUT       — SET_SCANOUT succeeded
VIRTIO_GPU_TRANSFER      — TRANSFER_TO_HOST_2D succeeded (fenced)
VIRTIO_GPU_FLUSH         — RESOURCE_FLUSH succeeded (fenced)
VIRTIO_GPU_TEST_PATTERN  — test pattern written + transferred + flushed
VIRTIO_GPU_UNREF         — UNREF_RESOURCE succeeded
VIRTIO_GPU_SELFTEST_OK   — full lifecycle self-test passed
VIRTIO_GPU_OK            — driver registered as gpudev:main
VIRTIO_GPU_IRQ           — first IRQ received

== ERROR HANDLING (typed errors with fallback) ==

- Bad response (non-OK response type): Err(InvalidState) + debug_print
- Missing feature (VIRGL/UUID/BLOB): rejected at negotiation, logged
- Queue exhaustion (free_capacity < needed): Err(Busy)
- Display event (VIRTIO_GPU_EVENT_DISPLAY): acked via events_clear, re-query
- Fence timeout (≥2s, FENCE_TIMEOUT_SPINS=2_000_000): Err(Timeout)
- Command timeout (~1s, CMD_TIMEOUT_SPINS=1_000_000): Err(Timeout)

== QEMU TEST INSTRUCTIONS ==

The virtio-gpu driver is auto-spawned by drivermgr phase-2 (userdisk bind
rules) when PCI discovers device 1af4:1050. To test:

  QEMU_EXTRA_ARGS="-device virtio-gpu-pci,max_outputs=1" \
    cargo xtask run

Or with the Python harness:

  QEMU_EXTRA_ARGS="-device virtio-gpu-pci,max_outputs=1" \
    python -m cluu_harness --case l2_login --no-build

The driver self-test creates a B8G8R8X8 resource, attaches a contiguous
DMA backing, sets scanout 0, writes a vertical gradient (orange→blue),
transfers to host (fenced), flushes (fenced), then unrefs. The test
pattern fills the entire scanout.

== PRE-EXISTING BUILD ISSUE ==

The full `cargo xtask build` fails at the `container-mp` (MicroPython)
step due to a pre-existing build output path mismatch unrelated to this
task. The virtio-gpu crate, container image, and init crate all build
successfully. The initrd assembly step does not run because the build
aborts at container-mp before reaching it.

== FEATURE NEGOTIATION ==

Accepted:  VIRTIO_F_VERSION_1 (bit 32), VIRTIO_GPU_F_EDID (bit 1, optional)
Rejected:  VIRTIO_GPU_F_VIRGL (bit 0), VIRTIO_GPU_F_RESOURCE_UUID (bit 2),
           VIRTIO_GPU_F_RESOURCE_BLOB (bit 3)

Classic 2D only. No blobs, no virgl, no rutabaga. Cursorq is set up but
no cursor commands are implemented (deferred per task spec).

== FENCE HANDLING ==

TRANSFER_TO_HOST_2D and RESOURCE_FLUSH use VIRTIO_GPU_FLAG_FENCE with a
monotonically increasing fence_id. The response fence_id is verified to
match the command fence_id. Fence timeout is ≥2s (FENCE_TIMEOUT_SPINS).

== EVENT PROCESSING ==

The driver reads GpuConfig.events_read on every IRQ and at self-test
start. If VIRTIO_GPU_EVENT_DISPLAY is set, it acks via events_clear and
re-queries GET_DISPLAY_INFO.
